{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
Jacob lay down with a stone for his pillow
In the wilderness alone
And he dreamed of [Am7]a ladder set upon [Fmaj7]the earth
Its top reaching up to [C]the throne
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
An[G]gels going up and down, going up and down
[Am]Surely the Lord is in this [F]place
And I did not [C]know it
An[G]gels going up and down
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
And the Lord stood above and said to [Fmaj7]him
I am with you wherever you [G]go
I will [Am]not leave you until I have [Fmaj7]done
All the things I [C]have promised you [G]so
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Angels going up and down, going up and down
Sure[Am]ly the Lord is in this place
[F]And I did not know [C]it
He is [G]in this place, and I did not know He was there
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
This [Am]is the house of God, this is [F]the gate of heaven
{end_of_verse}

